---
.title = "Retry HTTP failures and reuse connections",
.date = "2026-09-29",
.author = "ZigCC",
.layout = "section.shtml",
---

Transient server failures can be retried with a bounded attempt count. Keeping one
`std.http.Client` for all attempts also lets its connection pool reuse eligible keep-alive
connections; call `request.deinit()` after each response so the client can release or reuse it.
Only retry failures that are safe for the request and appropriate for the service.

